# 11. `Row` for Horizontal UI

Common uses:

* Icon + text
* Profile information
* Price + rating
* Buttons beside each other
* Navigation items
* Search bar + icon
* Country + flag
* Currency converter fields

Example:

```dart
Row(
  children: [
    Icon(Icons.flag),
    SizedBox(width: 8),
    Text("India"),
  ],
)
```

---

# 12. `Column` for Vertical UI

Common uses:

* Login forms
* Registration forms
* Profile screens
* Settings
* Product details
* Text + buttons
* Multiple input fields

Example:

```dart
Column(
  children: [
    TextField(),
    TextField(),
    ElevatedButton(
      onPressed: () {},
      child: Text("Login"),
    ),
  ],
)
```

---

# 13. `Row` Overflow Problem

A `Row` tries to keep its children on one horizontal line.

For example:

```dart
Row(
  children: [
    Text("Very very very long text..."),
    Text("Another long text..."),
    Text("More text..."),
  ],
)
```

This can cause:

```text
A RenderFlex overflowed...
```

The common solution is to use `Expanded` or `Flexible` when appropriate.

Example:

```dart
Row(
  children: [
    Expanded(
      child: Text(
        "Very long text that needs available space",
      ),
    ),
    Icon(Icons.more_vert),
  ],
)
```

We'll learn `Expanded` separately because it is **very important**.

---

# 14. Row vs Column

| Feature           | Row             | Column           |
| ----------------- | --------------- | ---------------- |
| Direction         | Horizontal      | Vertical         |
| Main axis         | Horizontal      | Vertical         |
| Cross axis        | Vertical        | Horizontal       |
| Multiple children | Yes             | Yes              |
| Uses `children`   | Yes             | Yes              |
| Common use        | Side-by-side UI | Top-to-bottom UI |

